# Canonical inventory format

`data/registers.json` uses schema version 1. Integer constants are JSON integers
or hexadecimal strings; unresolved critical constants are `null`. Source IDs
connect each `source_refs` item (`source`, `location`) to the root `sources`
array (`id`, `title`, `url`, `accessed`, optional revision and file hashes).

`blocks` contains datasheet functional blocks (`name`, `title`, `registers`).
Each register records `name`, `address`, `reset`, `storage_width`, `access`,
`description`, `evidence_status`, `source_refs`, `fields`, `writable_mask` and
`reserved_mask`. `notes` and `conflicts` retain qualifications and disagreements.
Root `conflicts` records candidate values, resolution and rationale; `coverage`
records the scope and limitations of the review.

Fields record `name`, `position`, `width`, unshifted `reset`, `access`,
`description`, `source_refs` and `enumerations`. An enumeration records `name`,
unshifted `value`, `description` and source locations. Reserved fields are marked
`reserved` or named `RESERVED...` and emit no field macros. A nonempty
`range_conflict` intentionally suppresses field position, width and mask macros.
Null register/field constants similarly suppress only the uncertain definition.

The prefix-only release embeds this inventory for audit; its renderer does not
parse it. The expanded templates already contain the reviewed metadata.
